From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:49:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] viuin: count the readers of each write-back channel

Both vdins shared one viuin frontend and both write-back channels one
state, so stopping one capture cleared the route of another capture of
the same tap and froze it. A failed start returned -1 and left its
frontend open. A v4l2 stop closed the frontend after fe_lock dropped,
or never when another driver such as amlvideo2 stopped vdin.
